type: software
title: "Commuting permutations with few joint orbits: asymptotics, log-concavity and the density of failures in every rank"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. A(l,n,k) counts the ordered l-tuples of pairwise commuting permutations of an n-element set with exactly k joint orbits. Abdesselam conjectured that k -> A(l,n,k) is log-concave for every rank l and every n; Starr disproved this at rank two at k = 2 and asked about higher rank. For every fixed rank l >= 2 and fixed k: the conjecture fails at two orbits in every rank, on a set of n of positive density, and holds at every fixed k >= 3 for large n; the exact limit inferior and superior of the log-concavity ratio are Euler products; the ratios have continuous limiting distributions, so the density of two-orbit failures exists (new also at rank two); explicit failures are certified in ranks three (a 54-digit n) and four (an 845-digit n). The proofs rest on an asymptotic formula with an explicit arithmetic factor and an explicit, uniform error term."
